cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Installor in research, teaching, or an industrial study, please cite this software."
title: "Installor"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-06
authors:
  - family-names: "Kumar"
    given-names: "Sudipta"
    alias: "the-sudipta"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-sudipta/installor"
url: "https://the-sudipta.github.io/installor/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Installor is a local-first, cross-platform desktop application for maintaining
  portable software catalogs, reviewing installed applications, acquiring and
  verifying installers, and executing explicit platform-native installation
  plans. It supports account-independent, read-only Google Sheet imports and an
  optional owner-deployed Apps Script bridge for bidirectional synchronization.
keywords:
  - software deployment
  - package management
  - software inventory
  - human-in-the-loop automation
  - software supply chain
  - Google Sheets
  - Tauri
  - Rust
